{"authored" [{"question" "q-316904" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the expression below, expressing your answer in the form $a+b\\text{i},$ where $a$ and $b$ are real numbers.\n\n$\\frac{5+2\\text{i}}{-2-3\\text{i}}=($\n{{field-1}} \n$)\\,+\\,($\n{{field-2}}\n$)\\,\\text{i}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951621/state.json" "file_sha256" "69da25893224e3d1cc9fcc1b30f69726906455e4758aa721fa0fec75e1e94027" "basis" 597 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951621/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-316904" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The denominator is $-2-3\\text{i}$ and its conjugate is $-2+3\\text{i}.$ We multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $-2+3\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5+2\\text{i}}{-2-3\\text{i}} & =\\frac{5+2\\text{i}}{-2-3\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{-2+3\\text{i}}{-2+3\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(5+2\\text{i})(-2+3\\text{i})}{(-2)^{2}-(3\\text{i})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-10+15\\text{i}-4\\text{i}+6{\\text{i}}^{2}}{4-(-9)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-10+11\\text{i}+6(-1)}{13} \\\\  & =\\frac{-16+11\\text{i}}{13}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-16+11\\text{i}}{13}=(-\\frac{16}{13})+(\\frac{11}{13})\\,\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951621/state.json" "file_sha256" "69da25893224e3d1cc9fcc1b30f69726906455e4758aa721fa0fec75e1e94027" "basis" 597 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951621/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-316904" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951621/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cadc02af78b9b71e4ac5e0bf9b7400e20f5fb16e2d1c725dfe56dd0a3eb9df24" "basis" 597 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951621/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-316904" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951621/state.json" "file_sha256" "69da25893224e3d1cc9fcc1b30f69726906455e4758aa721fa0fec75e1e94027" "basis" 597 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951621/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-316904" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951621/state.json" "file_sha256" "69da25893224e3d1cc9fcc1b30f69726906455e4758aa721fa0fec75e1e94027" "basis" 597 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951621/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-316848" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the expression below, expressing your answer in the form $a+b\\text{i},$ where $a$ and $b$ are real numbers.\n\n$\\frac{7\\text{i}}{3-\\text{i}}=($\n{{field-1}} \n$)\\,+\\,($\n{{field-2}}\n$)\\,\\text{i}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951621/state.json" "file_sha256" "69da25893224e3d1cc9fcc1b30f69726906455e4758aa721fa0fec75e1e94027" "basis" 597 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951621/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-316848" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The denominator is $3-\\text{i}$ and its conjugate is $3+\\text{i}.$ We multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $3+\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7\\text{i}}{3-\\text{i}} & =\\frac{7\\text{i}}{3-\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{3+\\text{i}}{3+\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{21\\text{i}+7{\\text{i}}^{2}}{{3}^{2}-(\\text{i})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{21\\text{i}+7(-1)}{9-(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-7+21\\text{i}}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{-7+21\\text{i}}{10}=(-\\frac{7}{10})+(\\frac{21}{10})\\,\\text{i}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951621/state.json" "file_sha256" "69da25893224e3d1cc9fcc1b30f69726906455e4758aa721fa0fec75e1e94027" "basis" 597 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951621/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-316848" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951621/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cadc02af78b9b71e4ac5e0bf9b7400e20f5fb16e2d1c725dfe56dd0a3eb9df24" "basis" 597 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951621/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-316848" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951621/state.json" "file_sha256" "69da25893224e3d1cc9fcc1b30f69726906455e4758aa721fa0fec75e1e94027" "basis" 597 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951621/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-316848" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{7}{10}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951621/state.json" "file_sha256" "69da25893224e3d1cc9fcc1b30f69726906455e4758aa721fa0fec75e1e94027" "basis" 597 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951621/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-316848" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951621/state.json" "file_sha256" "69da25893224e3d1cc9fcc1b30f69726906455e4758aa721fa0fec75e1e94027" "basis" 597 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951621/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-316848" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{21}{10}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951621/state.json" "file_sha256" "69da25893224e3d1cc9fcc1b30f69726906455e4758aa721fa0fec75e1e94027" "basis" 597 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951621/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-74648" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\frac{9}{-3+2\\text{i}}=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951621/state.json" "file_sha256" "69da25893224e3d1cc9fcc1b30f69726906455e4758aa721fa0fec75e1e94027" "basis" 597 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951621/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-74648" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The denominator is $-3+2\\text{i}$ and its conjugate is $-3-2\\text{i}.$ We multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $-3-2\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{9}{-3+2\\text{i}} & =\\frac{9}{-3+2\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{-3-2\\text{i}}{-3-2\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-27-18\\text{i}}{9+6\\text{i}-6\\text{i}-4{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-27-18\\text{i}}{9-4(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-27-18\\text{i}}{9+4} \\\\  & =\\frac{-27-18\\text{i}}{13}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-27-18\\text{i}}{13}=-\\frac{27}{13}-\\frac{18}{13}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951621/state.json" "file_sha256" "69da25893224e3d1cc9fcc1b30f69726906455e4758aa721fa0fec75e1e94027" "basis" 597 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951621/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-74648" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951621/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cadc02af78b9b71e4ac5e0bf9b7400e20f5fb16e2d1c725dfe56dd0a3eb9df24" "basis" 597 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951621/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-74648" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951621/state.json" "file_sha256" "69da25893224e3d1cc9fcc1b30f69726906455e4758aa721fa0fec75e1e94027" "basis" 597 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951621/edb-import/ver