" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{27}{13}-\\frac{18}{13}\\text{i}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951621/state.json" "file_sha256" "69da25893224e3d1cc9fcc1b30f69726906455e4758aa721fa0fec75e1e94027" "basis" 597 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951621/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-74659" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If ${z}_{1}=1-12\\text{i}$ and ${z}_{2}=8\\text{i}$, then ${z}_{1}$ divided by ${z}_{2}$ equals" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951621/state.json" "file_sha256" "69da25893224e3d1cc9fcc1b30f69726906455e4758aa721fa0fec75e1e94027" "basis" 597 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951621/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-74659" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we set up the fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1-12\\text{i}}{8\\text{i}}\n$$\n\nThe denominator is the imaginary number $8\\text{i}.$ Note that this can be written as $0+8\\text{i},$ so the conjugate is $0-8\\text{i},$ or simply $-8\\text{i}.$\n\nSo, we multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $-8\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{z}_{1}}{{z}_{2}} & =\\frac{1-12\\text{i}}{8\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-12\\text{i}}{8\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{-8\\text{i}}{-8\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-8\\text{i}+96{\\text{i}}^{2}}{-64{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-8\\text{i}+96(-1)}{-64(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-96-8\\text{i}}{64}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-96-8\\text{i}}{64}=-\\frac{96}{64}-\\frac{8}{64}\\text{i}=-\\frac{3}{2}-\\frac{1}{8}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951621/state.json" "file_sha256" "69da25893224e3d1cc9fcc1b30f69726906455e4758aa721fa0fec75e1e94027" "basis" 597 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951621/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-74659" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951621/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cadc02af78b9b71e4ac5e0bf9b7400e20f5fb16e2d1c725dfe56dd0a3eb9df24" "basis" 597 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951621/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-74659" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951621/state.json" "file_sha256" "69da25893224e3d1cc9fcc1b30f69726906455e4758aa721fa0fec75e1e94027" "basis" 597 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951621/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-74659" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{5}{8}\\text{i}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951621/state.json" "file_sha256" "69da25893224e3d1cc9fcc1b30f69726906455e4758aa721fa0fec75e1e94027" "basis" 597 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951621/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-74659" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{3}{2}-\\frac{1}{8}\\text{i}"] "category" "ma_