/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951621/state.json" "file_sha256" "69da25893224e3d1cc9fcc1b30f69726906455e4758aa721fa0fec75e1e94027" "basis" 597 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951621/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-316847" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the expression below, expressing your answer in the form $a+b\\text{i},$ where $a$ and $b$ are real numbers.\n\n$\\frac{5\\text{i}}{1+3\\text{i}}=($\n{{field-1}} \n$)\\,+\\,($\n{{field-2}}\n$)\\,\\text{i}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13970756/state.json" "file_sha256" "923efc918b6eb47397bc58e6c7ae4ec79d2edd400b79782b8446b570476b3508" "basis" 667 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13970756/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-316847" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The denominator is $1+3\\text{i}$ and its conjugate is $1-3\\text{i}.$ We multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $1-3\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5\\text{i}}{1+3\\text{i}} & =\\frac{5\\text{i}}{1+3\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{1-3\\text{i}}{1-3\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\text{i}-15{\\text{i}}^{2}}{{1}^{2}-(3\\text{i})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\text{i}-15(-1)}{1-(-9)} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\text{i}+15}{10} \\\\  & =\\frac{15+5\\text{i}}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{15+5\\text{i}}{10}=(\\frac{3}{2})+(\\frac{1}{2})\\,\\text{i}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13970756/state.json" "file_sha256" "923efc918b6eb47397bc58e6c7ae4ec79d2edd400b79782b8446b570476b3508" "basis" 667 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/C