ibute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13970756/state.json" "file_sha256" "923efc918b6eb47397bc58e6c7ae4ec79d2edd400b79782b8446b570476b3508" "basis" 667 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13970756/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-316756" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the expression below, expressing your answer in the form $a+b\\text{i},$ where $a$ and $b$ are real numbers.\n\n$\\frac{12-19\\text{i}}{8-11\\text{i}}=($\n{{field-1}} \n$)\\,+\\,($\n{{field-2}}\n$)\\,\\text{i}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037457/state.json" "file_sha256" "58f5edaf06cd6791fd9538b3fe60824e8e81fbf9036f0d7e894a6e906346c178"} {"question" "q-316756" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The denominator is $8-11\\text{i}$ and its conjugate is $8+11\\text{i}.$ We multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $8+11\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{12-19\\text{i}}{8-11\\text{i}} & =\\frac{12-19\\text{i}}{8-11\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{8+11\\text{i}}{8+11\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(12-19\\text{i})(8+11\\text{i})}{(8-11\\text{i})(8+11\\text{i})} \\\\  & =\\frac{96+132\\text{i}-152\\text{i}-209{\\text{i}}^{2}}{{8}^{2}-(11\\text{i})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{96-20\\text{i}-209(-1)}{{8}^{2}+{11}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{96-20\\text{i}+209}{64+121} \\\\  & =\\frac{305-20\\text{i}}{185} \\\\  & =\\frac{5(61-4\\text{i})}{5\\cdot 37} \\\\  & =\\frac{61-4\\text{i}}{37}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{61-4\\text{i}}{37}=(\\frac{61}{37})+(-\\frac{4}{37})\\,\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037457/state.json" "file_sha256" "58f5edaf06cd6791fd9538b3fe60824e8e81fbf9036f0d7e894a6e906346c178"} {"question" "q-316756" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037457/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c494780e4970659270872b5cd5b1ab0e6be9b4fef0c02cbecb5ab0822ce4b831"} {"question" "q-316756" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037457/state.json" "file_sha256" "58f5edaf06cd6791fd9538b3fe60824e8e81fbf9036f0d7e894a6e906346c178"} {"question" "q-316756" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{61}{37}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037457/state.json" "file_sha256" "58f5edaf06cd6791fd9538b3fe60824e8e81fbf9036f0d7e894a6e906346c178"} {"question" "q-316756" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037457/state.json" "file_sha256" "58f5edaf06cd6791fd9538b3fe60824e8e81fbf9036f0d7e894a6e906346c178"} {"question" "q-316756" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{4}{37}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037457/state.json" "file_sha256" "58f5edaf06cd6791fd9538b3fe60824e8e81fbf9036f0d7e894a6e906346c178"} {"question" "q-16431" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "if ${z}_{1}=5+5\\text{i}$ and ${z}_{2}=-3+8\\text{i}$, then ${z}_{1}$ divided by ${z}_{2}$ equals" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037457/state.json" "file_sha256" "58f5edaf06cd6791fd9538b3fe60824e8e81fbf9036f0d7e894a6e906346c178"} {"question" "q-16431" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we set up the fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{5+5\\text{i}}{-3+8\\text{i}}\n$$\n\nThe denominator is $-3+8\\text{i}$ and its conjugate is $-3-8\\text{i}.$ We multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $-3-8\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{z}_{1}}{{z}_{2}} & =\\frac{5+5\\text{i}}{-3+8\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5+5\\text{i}}{-3+8\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{-3-8\\text{i}}{-3-8\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-15-40\\text{i}-15\\text{i}-40{\\text{i}}^{2}}{{3}^{2}-{8}^{2}{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-15-55\\text{i}-40(-1)}{{3}^{2}+{8}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-15-55\\text{i}+40}{9+64} \\\\  & =\\frac{25-55\\text{i}}{73}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{25-55\\text{i}}{73}=\\frac{25}{73}-\\frac{55}{73}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037457/state.json" "file_sha256" "58f5edaf06cd6791fd9538b3fe60824e8e81fbf9036f0d7e894a6e906346c178"} {"question" "q-16431" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037457/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c494780e4970659270872b5cd5b1ab0e6be9b4fef0c02cbecb5ab0822ce4b831"} {"question" "q-16431" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037457/state.json" "file_sha256" "58f5edaf06cd6791fd9538b3fe60824e8e81fbf9036f0d7e894a6e906346c178"} {"question" "q-16431" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{25}{73}-\\frac{55}{73}\\text{i}"] ["math" "-\\frac{73}{25}+\\frac{55}{73}\\text{i}"] ["math" "-\\frac{73}{25}-\\frac{55}{73}\\text{i}"] ["math" "\\frac{25}{73}+\\frac{55}{73}\\text{i}"] ["math" "\\frac{25}{73}-\\frac{55}{73}\\text{i}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037457/state.json" "file_sha256" "58f5edaf06cd6791fd9538b3fe60824e8e81fbf9036f0d7e894a6e906346c178"} {"question" "q-16431" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{25}{73}-\\frac{55}{73}\\text{i}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037457/state.json" "file_sha256" "58f5edaf06cd6791fd9538b3fe60824e8e81fbf9036f0d7e894a6e906346c178"} {"question" "q-316904" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the expression below, expressing your answer in the form $a+b\\text{i},$ where $a$ and $b$ are real numbers.\n\n$\\frac{5+2\\text{i}}{-2-3\\text{i}}=($\n{{field-1}} \n$)\\,+\\,($\n{{field-2}}\n$)\\,\\text{i}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037457/state.json" "file_sha256" "58f5edaf06cd6791fd9538b3fe60824e8e81fbf9036f0d7e894a6e906346c178"} {"question" "q-316904" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The denominator is $-2-3\\text{i}$ and its conjugate is $-2+3\\text{i}.$ We multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $-2+3\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5+2\\text{i}}{-2-3\\text{i}} & =\\frac{5+2\\text{i}}{-2-3\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{-2+3\\text{i}}{-2+3\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(5+2\\text{i})(-2+3\\text{i})}{(-2)^{2}-(3\\text{i})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-10+15\\text{i}-4\\text{i}+6{\\text{i}}^{2}}{4-(-9)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-10+11\\text{i}+6(-1)}{13} \\\\  & =\\frac{-16+11\\text{i}}{13}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-16+11\\text{i}}{13}=(-\\frac{16}{13})+(\\frac{11}{13})\\,\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037457/state.json" "file_sha256" "58f5edaf06cd6791fd9538b3fe60824e8e81fbf9036f0d7e894a6e906346c178"} {"question" "q-316904" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037457/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c494780e4970659270872b5cd5b1ab0e6be9b4fef0c02cbecb5ab0822ce4b831"} {"question" "q-316904" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037457/state.json" "file_sha256" "58f5edaf06cd6791fd9538b3fe60824e8e81fbf9036f0d7e894a6e906346c178"} {"question" "q-316904" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{16}{13}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037457/state.json" "file_sha256" "58f5edaf06cd6791fd9538b3fe60824e8e81fbf9036f0d7e894a6e906346c178"} {"question" "q-316904" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037457/state.json" "file_sha256" "58f5edaf06cd6791fd9538b3fe60824e8e81fbf9036f0d7e894a6e906346c178"} {"question" "q-316904" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{11}{13}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037457/state.json" "file_sha256" "58f5edaf06cd6791fd9538b3fe60824e8e81fbf9036f0d7e894a6e906346c178"} {"question" "q-167671" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\frac{5-2\\text{i}}{1+2\\text{i}}=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037457/state.json" "file_sha256" "58f5edaf06cd6791fd9538b3fe60824e8e81fbf9036f0d7e894a6e906346c178"} {"question" "q-167671" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The denominator is $1+2\\text{i}$ and its conjugate is $1-2\\text{i}.$ We multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $1-2\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5-2\\text{i}}{1+2\\text{i}} & =\\frac{5-2\\text{i}}{1+2\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{1-2\\text{i}}{1-2\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5-10\\text{i}-2\\text{i}+4{\\text{i}}^{2}}{{1}^{2}-{2}^{2}{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5-12\\text{i}+4(-1)}{1-4(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{5-12\\text{i}-4}{1+4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-12\\text{i}}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{1-12\\text{i}}{5}=\\frac{1}{5}-\\frac{12}{5}\\text{i}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037457/state.json" "file_sha256" "58f5edaf06cd6791fd9538b3fe60824e8e81fbf9036f0d7e894a6e9063