d" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we set up the fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{2-5\\text{i}}{6+3\\text{i}}\n$$\n\nThe denominator is $6+3\\text{i}$ and its conjugate is $6-3\\text{i}.$ We multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $6-3\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{z}_{1}}{{z}_{2}} & =\\frac{2-5\\text{i}}{6+3\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2-5\\text{i}}{6+3\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{6-3\\text{i}}{6-3\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{12-6\\text{i}-30\\text{i}+15{\\text{i}}^{2}}{{6}^{2}-{3}^{2}{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{12-36\\text{i}+15(-1)}{{6}^{2}+{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{12-36\\text{i}-15}{36+9} \\\\  & =\\frac{-3-36\\text{i}}{45}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-3-36\\text{i}}{45}=-\\frac{3}{45}-\\frac{36}{45}\\text{i}=-\\frac{1}{15}-\\frac{4}{5}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037457/state.json" "file_sha256" "58f5edaf06cd6791fd9538b3fe60824e8e81fbf9036f0d7e894a6e906346c178"} {"question" "q-964" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037457/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c494780e4970659270872b5cd5b1ab0e6be9b4fef0c02cbecb5ab0822ce4b831"} {"question" "q-964" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037457/state.json" "file_sha256" "58f5edaf06cd6791fd9538b3fe60824e8e81fbf9036f0d7e894a6e906346c178"} {"question" "q-964" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answ