olution" "value" "The denominator is $1+\\text{i}$ and its conjugate is $1-\\text{i}.$ We multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $1-\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3\\text{i}}{1+\\text{i}} & =\\frac{3\\text{i}}{1+\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{1-\\text{i}}{1-\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\text{i}-3{\\text{i}}^{2}}{{1}^{2}-{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\text{i}-3(-1)}{1-(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\text{i}+3}{1+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\text{i}+3}{2}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3\\text{i}+3}{2}=\\frac{3}{2}+\\frac{3}{2}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037457/state.json" "file_sha256" "58f5edaf06cd6791fd9538b3fe60824e8e81fbf9036f0d7e894a6e906346c178"} {"question" "q-963" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037457/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c494780e4970659270872b5cd5b1ab0e6be9b4fef0c02cbecb5ab0822ce4b831"} {"question" "q-963" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037457/state.json" "file_sha256" "58f5edaf06cd6791fd9538b3fe60824e8e81fbf9036f0d7e894a6e906346c178"} {"question" "q-963" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{3}{2}-\\frac{3}{2}\\text{i}"] ["math" "3+3\\text{i}"] ["math" "3-3\\text{i}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{2}+\\frac{3}{2}\\text{i}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{2}-\\frac{3}{2}\\text{i}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037457/state.json" "file_sha256" "58f5edaf06cd6791fd9538b3fe60824e8e81fbf9036f0d7e894a6e906346c178"} {"question" "q-963" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{2}+\\frac{3}{2}\\text{i}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037457/state.json" "file_sha256" "58f5edaf06cd6791fd9538b3fe60824e8e81fbf9036f0d7e894a6e906346c178"} {"question" "q-316865" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the expression below, expressing your answer in the form $a+b\\text{i},$ where $a$ and $b$ are real numbers.\n\n$\\frac{-6}{3+2\\text{i}}=($\n {{field-1}} \n$)\\,+\\,($\n{{field-2}}\n$)\\,\\text{i}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037457/state.json" "file_sha256" "58f5edaf06cd6791fd9538b3fe60824e8e81fbf9036f0d7e894a6e906346c178"} {"question" "q-316865" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The denominator is $3+2\\text{i}$ and its conjugate is $3-2\\text{i}.$ We multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $3-2\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-6}{3+2\\text{i}} & =\\frac{-6}{3+2\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{3-2\\text{i}}{3-2\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-18+12\\text{i}}{{3}^{2}-(2\\text{i})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-18+12\\text{i}}{9-(-4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-18+12\\text{i}}{13}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-18+12\\text{i}}{13}=(-\\frac{18}{13})+(\\frac{12}{13})\\,\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037457/state.json" "file_sha256" "58f5edaf06cd6791fd9538b3fe60824e8e81fbf9036f0d7e894a6e906346c178"} {"question" "q-316865" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037457/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c494780e4970659270872b5cd5b1ab0e6be9b4fef0c02cbecb5ab0822ce4b831"} {"question" "q-316865" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037457/state.json" "file_sha256" "58f5edaf06cd6791fd9538b3fe60824e8e81fbf9036f0d7e894a6e906346c178"} {"question" "q-316865" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{18}{13}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037457/state.json" "file_sha256" "58f5edaf06cd6791fd9538b3fe60824e8e81fbf9036f0d7e894a6e906346c178"} {"question" "q-316865" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037457/state.json" "file_sha256" "58f5edaf06cd6791fd9538b3fe60824e8e81fbf9036f0d7e894a6e906346c178"} {"question" "q-316865" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{12}{13}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037457/state.json" "file_sha256" "58f5edaf06cd6791fd9538b3fe60824e8e81fbf9036f0d7e894a6e906346c178"} {"question" "q-74648" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\frac{9}{-3+2\\text{i}}=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037457/state.json" "file_sha256" "58f5edaf06cd6791fd9538b3fe60824e8e81fbf9036f0d7e894a6e906346c178"} {"question" "q-74648" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The denominator is $-3+2\\text{i}$ and its conjugate is $-3-2\\text{i}.$ We multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $-3-2\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{9}{-3+2\\text{i}} & =\\frac{9}{-3+2\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{-3-2\\text{i}}{-3-2\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-27-18\\text{i}}{9+6\\text{i}-6\\text{i}-4{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-27-18\\text{i}}{9-4(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-27-18\\text{i}}{9+4} \\\\  & =\\frac{-27-18\\text{i}}{13}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-27-18\\text{i}}{13}=-\\frac{27}{13}-\\frac{18}{13}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037457/state.json" "file_sha256" "58f5edaf06cd6791fd9538b3fe60824e8e81fbf9036f0d7e894a6e906346c178"} {"question" "q-74648" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037457/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c494780e4970659270872b5cd5b1ab0e6be9b4fef0c02cbecb5ab0822ce4b831"} {"question" "q-74648" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037457/state.json" "file_sha256" "58f5edaf06cd6791fd9538b3fe60824e8e81fbf9036f0d7e894a6e906346c178"} {"question" "q-74648" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{18}{13}-\\frac{27}{13}\\text{i}"] ["math" "-\\frac{27}{13}+\\frac{18}{13}\\text{i}"] ["math" "-\\frac{27}{13}-\\frac{18}{13}\\text{i}"] ["math" "\\frac{27}{13}+\\frac{18}{13}\\text{i}"] ["math" "\\frac{27}{13}-\\frac{18}{13}\\text{i}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037457/state.json" "file_sha256" "58f5edaf06cd6791fd9538b3fe60824e8e81fbf9036f0d7e894a6e906346c178"} {"question" "q-74648" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{27}{13}-\\frac{18}{13}\\text{i}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037457/state.json" "file_sha256" "58f5edaf06cd6791fd9538b3fe60824e8e81fbf9036f0d7e894a6e906346c178"} {"question" "q-275375" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the expression below, expressing your answer in the form $a+b\\text{i},$ where $a$ and $b$ are real numbers.\n\n$\\frac{-4}{2-6\\text{i}}=($\n{{field-1}} \n$)\\,+\\,($\n{{field-2}}\n$)\\,\\text{i}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037457/state.json" "file_sha256" "58f5edaf06cd6791fd9538b3fe60824e8e81fbf9036f0d7e894a6e906346c178"} {"question" "q-275375" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The denominator is $2-6\\text{i}$ and its conjugate is $2+6\\text{i}.$ We multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $2+6\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-4}{2-6\\text{i}} & =\\frac{-4}{2-6\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{2+6\\text{i}}{2+6\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-8-24\\text{i}}{4+12\\text{i}-12\\text{i}-36{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-8-24\\text{i}}{4-36{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-8-24\\text{i}}{4-(36)(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-8-24\\text{i}}{4+36} \\\\  & =\\frac{-8-24\\text{i}}{40}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-8-24\\text{i}}{40}=-\\frac{8}{40}-\\frac{24}{40}\\text{i}=(-\\frac{1}{5})+(-\\frac{3}{5})\\,\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037457/state.json" "file_sha256" "58f5edaf06cd6791fd9538b3fe60824e8e81fbf9036f0d7e894a6e906346c178"} {"question" "q-275375" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037457/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c494780e4970659270872b5cd5b1ab0e6be9b4fef0c02cbecb5ab0822ce4b831"} {"question" "q-275375" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037457/state.json" "file_sha256" "58f5edaf06cd6791fd9538b3fe60824e8e81fbf9036f0d7e894a6e906346c178"} {"question" "q-275375" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{1}{5}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037457/state.json" "file_sha256" "58f5edaf06cd6791fd9538b3fe60824e8e81fbf9036f0d7e894a6e906346c178"} {"question" "q-275375" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037457/state.json" "file_sha256" "58f5edaf06cd6791fd9538b3fe60824e8e81fbf9036f0d7e894a6e906346c178"} {"question" "q-275375" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{3}{5}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037457/state.json" "file_sha256" "58f5edaf06cd6791fd9538b3fe60824e8e81fbf9036f0d7e894a6e906346c178"} {"question" "q-74649" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\frac{-10}{4+3\\text{i}}=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037457/state.json" "file_sha256" "58f5edaf06cd6791fd9538b3fe60824e8e81fbf9036f0d7e894a6e906346c178"} {"question" "q-74649" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The denominator is $4+3\\text{i}$ and its conjugate is $4-3\\text{i}.$ We multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $4-3\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-10}{4+3\\text{i}} & =\\frac{-10}{4+3\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{4-3\\text{i}}{4-3\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-40+30\\text{i}}{16-12\\text{i}+12\\text{i}-9{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-40+30\\text{i}}{16-9{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-40+30\\text{i}}{16-(9)(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-40+30\\text{i}}{16+9} \\\\  & =\\frac{-40+30\\text{i}}{25}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-40+30\\text{i}}{25}=-\\frac{40}{25}+\\frac{30}{25}\\text{i}=-\\frac{8}{5}+\\frac{6}{5}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037457/state.json" "file_sha256" "58f5edaf06cd6791fd9538b3fe60824e8e81fbf9036f0d7e894a6e906346c178"} {"question" "q-74649" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jak