7\\text{i}}{2\\text{i}}=($\n{{field-1}} \n$)\\,+\\,($\n{{field-2}}\n$)\\,\\text{i}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037457/state.json" "file_sha256" "58f5edaf06cd6791fd9538b3fe60824e8e81fbf9036f0d7e894a6e906346c178"} {"question" "q-316888" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Here, the denominator is the imaginary number $2\\text{i}.$ Note that this can be written as $0+2\\text{i},$ so the conjugate is $0-2\\text{i},$ or simply $-2\\text{i}.$\n\nSo, we multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $-2\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-6-7\\text{i}}{2\\text{i}} & =\\frac{-6-7\\text{i}}{2\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{-2\\text{i}}{-2\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{12\\text{i}+14{\\text{i}}^{2}}{-4{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{12\\text{i}+14(-1)}{-4(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-14+12\\text{i}}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-14+12\\text{i}}{4} & =-\\frac{14}{4}+\\frac{12}{4}\\text{i} \\\\  & =(-\\frac{7}{2})+(3)\\,\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037457/state.json" "file_sha256" "58f5edaf06cd6791fd9538b3fe60824e8e81fbf9036f0d7e894a6e906346c178"} {"question" "q-316888" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037457/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c494780e4970659270872b5cd5b1ab0e6be9b4fef0c02cbecb5ab0822ce4b831"} {"question" "q-316888" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037457/state.json" "file_sha256" "58f5edaf06cd6791fd9538b3fe60824e8e81fbf9036f0d7e894a6e906346c178"} {"question" "q-316888" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{7}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037457/state.json" "file_sha256" "58f5edaf06cd6791fd9538b3fe60824e8e81fbf9036f0d7e894a6e906346c178"} {"question" "q-316888" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037457/state.json" "file_sha256" "58f5edaf06cd6791fd9538b3fe60824e8e81fbf9036f0d7e894a6e906346c178"} {"question" "q-316888" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037457/state.json" "file_sha256" "58f5edaf06cd6791fd9538b3fe60824e8e81fbf9036f0d7e894a6e906346c178"} {"question" "e-5780" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Express $\\dfrac {4 + \\textrm{i}} {1 - \\textrm{i}}$ in the form $a+\\textrm{i}b.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037457/example-5780.json" "file_sha256" "54132cb20ea124742f5da7096f0a2120db5c42beb580f3ae7c20932a787f3ef6"} {"question" "e-5780" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The denominator is $1-\\textrm{i}$ and its conjugate is $1+\\textrm{i}.$ We multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $1+\\textrm{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\dfrac {4 + \\textrm{i}} {1 - \\textrm{i}} \n&=\\dfrac {4 + \\textrm{i}} {1 - \\textrm{i}} \\cdot \\dfrac {1 + \\textrm{i}} {1 + \\textrm{i}}  \\[5pt]\n&= \\dfrac {4 + 4\\textrm{i} + \\textrm{i} + \\textrm{i}^2} {1^2 - \\textrm{i}^2}  \\[5pt]\n&= \\dfrac {4 + 5\\textrm{i} + (-1)} {1 - (-1)}  \\[5pt]\n&= \\dfrac {3 + 5\\textrm{i}} {2}\t\n\t}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+\\textrm{i} b \\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\dfrac {3 + 5\\textrm{i}} {2} =\n\t\t\\dfrac{3} {2} + \\dfrac {5} {2} \\textrm{i}\t\n\t}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037457/example-5780.json" "file_sha256" "54132cb20ea124742f5da7096f0a2120db5c42beb580f3ae7c20932a787f3ef6"} {"question" "e-6230" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $z_1=3\\textrm{i}$ and $z_2 = 2+5\\textrm{i},$ then what is $z_1$ divided by $z_2?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037457/example-6230.json" "file_sha256" "49f5ef2e28b220d896f9f0ab04760b7622724bd320c3c8813e1e8ff1d7d84254"} {"question" "e-6230" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we set up the fraction:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{3\\textrm{i}}{2+5\\textrm i}\n$$\n\nThe denominator is $2+5\\textrm{i}$ and its conjugate is $2-5\\textrm{i}.$ We multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $2-5\\textrm{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\dfrac {3 \\textrm{i}} {2 +5\\textrm{i}} \n&= \\dfrac {3 \\textrm{i}} {2 +5 \\textrm{i}} \\cdot \\dfrac {2 -5 \\textrm{i}} {2-5\\textrm{i}}  \\[5pt]\n&=\\dfrac {6 \\textrm{i} - 15 \\textrm{i}^2 } {2^2 - (5\\textrm{i})^2}  \\[5pt]\n&=\\dfrac {6 \\textrm{i} - 15\\textrm{i}^2 } {4 - 25\\textrm{i}^2} \\[5pt]\n&= \\dfrac {6 \\textrm{i} - 15(-1) } {4 - 25(-1)}  \\[5pt]\n&=\\dfrac {6 \\textrm{i} + 15 } {29}\n\t}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b \\textrm{i}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\dfrac {6 \\textrm{i} + 15 } {29}=\n\t\t\\dfrac{15} {29} + \\dfrac {6} {29} \\textrm{i}\t\n\t}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037457/example-6230.json" "file_sha256" "49f5ef2e28b220d896f9f0ab04760b7622724bd320c3c8813e1e8ff1d7d84254"} {"question" "e-6231" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Express $\\dfrac{4}{-1+2\\textrm{i} }$ in the form $a+\\textrm{i}b.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037457/example-6231.json" "file_sha256" "ab8d687b7c9f2cbd39d15b7ce051c4450598d8c9090d0fd704443581b4ff2608"} {"question" "e-6231" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The denominator is $-1+2\\textrm{i}$ and its conjugate is $-1-2\\textrm{i}.$ We multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $-1-2\\textrm{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\dfrac {4} {-1 +2\\textrm{i}} \n&=\\dfrac {4} {-1 +2 \\textrm{i}} \\cdot \\dfrac {-1 -2 \\textrm{i}} {-1-2\\textrm{i}}  \\[5pt]\n&= \\dfrac {-4 - 8 \\textrm{i} } {(-1)^2 - (2\\textrm{i})^2}  \\[5pt]\n&= \\dfrac {-4 - 8 \\textrm{i} } {1 - 4\\textrm{i}^2}  \\[5pt]\n&= \\dfrac {-4 - 8 \\textrm{i} } {1 - 4(-1)}  \\[5pt]\n&= \\dfrac {-4 - 8 \\textrm{i} } {5} \n\t}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b \\textrm{i}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\dfrac {-4 - 8 \\textrm{i} } {5} =\n\t\t-\\dfrac{4} {5} - \\dfrac {8} {5} \\textrm{i}\t\n\t}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037457/example-6231.json" "file_sha256" "ab8d687b7c9f2cbd39d15b7ce051c4450598d8c9090d0fd704443581b4ff2608"} {"question" "e-5781" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $z_1 = -8-3\\textrm{i}$ and $z_2 = 2\\textrm{i},$ then what is $z_1$ divided by $z_2?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037457/example-5781.json" "file_sha256" "3af6759ecb851ea27712239da2e445a8f478c62b48feef192b243211433cd1ba"} {"question" "e-5781" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we set up the fraction:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac {-8 - 3\\textrm{i}} {2\\textrm{i}}\n$$\n\nThe denominator is the imaginary number $2\\textrm{i}.$ Note that this can be written as $0+2\\textrm{i},$ so the conjugate is $0-2\\textrm{i},$ or simply $-2\\textrm{i}.$\n\nSo, we multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $-2\\textrm{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\dfrac {-8 - 3\\textrm{i}} {2\\textrm{i}} \n&= \t\\dfrac {-8 - 3\\textrm{i}} {2\\textrm{i}} \\cdot \\dfrac {-2\\textrm{i}} {-2\\textrm{i}} \\[5pt]\n&= \t\\dfrac {16\\textrm{i} + 6\\textrm{i}^2} {-4\\textrm{i}^2} \\[5pt]\n&= \t\\dfrac {16\\textrm{i} + 6(-1)} {-4(-1)} \\[5pt]\n&= \t\\dfrac {-6 + 16\\textrm{i}} {4}\t\t\t\n\t}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b \\textrm{i}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\dfrac {-6 + 16\\textrm{i}} {4} &= - \\dfrac{6}{4} + \\dfrac{16}{4} \\textrm{i} \\[5pt]\n&=\t\t-\\dfrac{3} {2} + 4\\textrm{i}\t\t\t\t\n\t}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037457/example-5781.json" "file_sha256" "3af6759ecb851ea27712239da2e445a8f478c62b48feef192b243211433cd1ba"}] "usage" {"q-74648" [] "q-963" [] "e-5781" [] "e-6230" [] "q-964" [] "q-316847" [] "q-74659" [] "q-316904" [] "q-316848" [] "e-6231" [] "e-5780" []} "basis" 1511 "retractions" [[17592186060371 :question/problem "If $z_{1} = 2 - 5\\textrm{i}$ and $z_{2} = 6 + 3\\textrm{i}$, then $z_{1}$ divided by $z_{2}$ equals"] [17592186060370 :question/problem "What is $\\frac{3\\textrm{i}}{1 + \\textrm{i}}$?"] [17592186059528 :question/problem "Express $\\dfrac {4 + \\textrm{i}} {1 - \\textrm{i}}$ in the form $a+\\textrm{i}b$."] [17592186059528 :question/worked-solution "The denominator is $1-\\textrm{i}$ and its conjugate is $1+\\textrm{i}$. We multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $1+\\textrm{i}$, so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} \\dfrac {4 + \\textrm{i}} {1 - \\textrm{i}} &=\\dfrac {4 + \\textrm{i}} {1 - \\textrm{i}} \\cdot \\dfrac {1 + \\textrm{i}} {1 + \\textrm{i}} \\\\[5pt] &= \\dfrac {4 + 4\\textrm{i} + \\textrm{i} + \\textrm{i}^2} {1^2 - \\textrm{i}^2} \\\\[5pt] &= \\dfrac {4 + 5\\textrm{i} + (-1)} {1 - (-1)} \\\\[5pt] &= \\dfrac {3 + 5\\textrm{i}} {2} \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+\\textrm{i} b$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} \\dfrac {3 + 5\\textrm{i}} {2} = \\dfrac{3} {2} + \\dfrac {5} {2} \\textrm{i} \\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186059530 :question/problem "If $z_1=3\\textrm{i}$ and $z_2 = 2+5\\textrm{i}$, then what is $z_1$ divided by $z_2$?"] [17592186059530 :question/worked-solution "First, we set up the fraction:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{3\\textrm{i}}{2+5\\textrm i}\n$$\n\nThe denominator is $2+5\\textrm{i}$ and its conjugate is $2-5\\textrm{i}$. We multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $2-5\\textrm{i}$, so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} \\dfrac {3 \\textrm{i}} {2 +5\\textrm{i}} &= \\dfrac {3 \\textrm{i}} {2 +5 \\textrm{i}} \\cdot \\dfrac {2 -5 \\textrm{i}} {2-5\\textrm{i}} \\\\[5pt] &=\\dfrac {6 \\textrm{i} - 15 \\textrm{i}^2} {2^2 - (5\\textrm{i})^2} \\\\[5pt] &=\\dfrac {6 \\textrm{i} - 15\\textrm{i}^2} {4 - 25\\textrm{i}^2} \\\\[5pt] &= \\dfrac {6 \\textrm{i} - 15(-1)} {4 - 25(-1)} \\\\[5pt] &=\\dfrac {6 \\textrm{i} + 15} {29} \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b \\textrm{i}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} \\dfrac {6 \\textrm{i} + 15} {29}= \\dfrac{15} {29} + \\dfrac {6} {29} \\textrm{i} \\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186059531 :question/problem "Express $\\dfrac{4}{-1+2\\textrm{i}}$ in the form $a+\\textrm{i}b$."] [17592186059531 :question/worked-solution "The denominator is $-1+2\\textrm{i}$ and its conjugate is $-1-2\\textrm{i}$. We multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $-1-2\\textrm{i}$, so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} \\dfrac {4} {-1 +2\\textrm{i}} &=\\dfrac {4} {-1 +2 \\textrm{i}} \\cdot \\dfrac {-1 -2 \\textrm{i}} {-1-2\\textrm{i}} \\\\[5pt] &= \\dfrac {-4 - 8 \\textrm{i}} {(-1)^2 - (2\\textrm{i})^2} \\\\[5pt] &= \\dfrac {-4 - 8 \\textrm{i}} {1 - 4\\textrm{i}^2} \\\\[5pt] &= \\dfrac {-4 - 8 \\textrm{i}} {1 - 4(-1)} \\\\[5pt] &= \\dfrac {-4 - 8 \\textrm{i}} {5} \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b \\textrm{i}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} \\dfrac {-4 - 8 \\textrm{i}} {5} = -\\dfrac{4} {5} - \\dfrac {8} {5} \\textrm{i} \\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186059529 :question/problem "If $z_1 = -8-3\\textrm{i}$ and $z_2 = 2\\textrm{i}$, then what is $z_1$ divided by $z_2$?"] [17592186059529 :question/worked-solution "First, we set up the fraction:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac {-8 - 3\\textrm{i}} {2\\textrm{i}}\n$$\n\nThe denominator is the imaginary number $2\\textrm{i}$. Note that this can be written as $0+2\\textrm{i}$, so the conjugate is $0-2\\textrm{i}$, or simply $-2\\textrm{i}$.\n\nSo, we multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $-2\\textrm{i}$, so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} \\dfrac {-8 - 3\\textrm{i}} {2\\textrm{i}} &= \\dfrac {-8 - 3\\textrm{i}} {2\\textrm{i}} \\cdot \\dfrac {-2\\textrm{i}} {-2\\textrm{i}} \\\\[5pt] &= \\dfrac {16\\textrm{i} + 6\\textrm{i}^2} {-4\\textrm{i}^2} \\\\[5pt] &= \\dfrac {16\\textrm{i} + 6(-1)} {-4(-1)} \\\\[5pt] &= \\dfrac {-6 + 16\\textrm{i}} {4} \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b \\textrm{i}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} \\dfrac {-6 + 16\\textrm{i}} {4} &=-\\dfrac{6}{4} + \\dfrac{16}{4} \\textrm{i} \\\\[5pt] &= -\\dfrac{3} {2} + 4\\textrm{i} \\end{aligned}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186059204 17592186059205 17592186059206 17592186059207 17592186059208 17592186059210 17592186059211 17592186059212 17592186059213 17592186059214 17592186265139 17592186265141 17592186265181 17592186265182 17592186265184 17592186265208 17592186265209 17592186265210 17592186265211 17592186265212 17592186265215 17592186265216 17592186265217 17592186265218 17592186265219 17592186275630 17592186275632] "immutable_fields" [[17592186059203 :answer-field/correct] [17592186059203 :answer-field/id] [17592186059203 :answer-field/key] [17592186059203 :answer-field/type] [17592186059209 :answer-field/correct] [17592186059209 :answer-field/id] [17592186059209 :answer-field/key] [17592186059209 :answer-field/type] [17592186265138 :answer-field/correct] [17592186265138 :answer-field/id] [17592186265138 :answer-field/key] [17592186265138 :answer-field/type] [17592186265140 :answer-field/correct] [17592186265140 :answer-field/id] [17592186265140 :answer-field/key] [17592186265140 :answer-field/type] [17592186265180 :answer-field/correct] [17592186265180 :answer-field/id] [17592186265180 :answer-field/key] [17592186265180 :answer-field/type] [17592186265183 :answer-field/correct] [17592186265183 :answer-field/id] [17592186265183 :answer-field/key] [17592186265183 :answer-field/type] [17592186265207 :answer-field/correct] [17592186265207 :answer-field/id] [17592186265207 :answer-field/key] [17592186265207 :answer-field/type] [17592186265214 :answer-field/correct] [17592186265214 :answer-field/id] [17592186265214 :answer-field/key] [17592186265214 :answer-field/type] [17592186275629 :answer-field/correct] [17592186275629 :answer-field/id] [17592186275629 :answer-field/key] [17592186275629 :answer-field/type] [17